<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding the mistake in a sine calculation</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Achieng was told that \(\cos x = {@g@}\) and \({@intv@}\). She found \(\sin x\) like this. Her working has one mistake.</p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;"><tr><td style="padding:3px 12px;">Step 1</td><td>\(\sin^2 x = 1 - \cos^2 x\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:3px 12px;">Step 2</td><td>[[if test="is(er = 1)"]]\(\sin^2 x = 1 - ({@g@}) = {@dispdp(1-g,4)@}\)[[else]]\(\sin^2 x = 1 - ({@g@})^2 = {@dispdp(v2,4)@}\)[[/if]]</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:3px 12px;">Step 3</td><td>[[if test="is(er = 2)"]]\(\sin x = \pm {@dispdp(v2,4)@}\)[[else]]\(\sin x = \pm\sqrt{ {@dispdp(s2,4)@} } = \pm {@dispdp(s3,4)@}\)[[/if]]</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:3px 12px;">Step 4</td><td>\(x\) is in the {@qword@} quadrant, so \(\sin x = {@dispdp(s4,4)@}\)</td></tr></table><p>(a) Which step has the mistake?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Give the correct value of \(\sin x\).</p><div>\(\sin x =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\sin^2 x = 1 - \cos^2 x = 1 - ({@g@})^2 = {@dispdp(v2,4)@}\), so \(\sin x = \pm\sqrt{ {@dispdp(v2,4)@} } = \pm {@dispdp(abs(sv),4)@}\).</p><p>\(x\) is in the {@qword@} quadrant, where \(\sin x\) is {@sword@}: \(\sin x = {@dispdp(sv,4)@}\).</p><p>[[if test="is(er = 1)"]]Achieng's mistake is in step 2: she subtracted \(\cos x\), not \(\cos^2 x\).[[/if]][[if test="is(er = 2)"]]Achieng's mistake is in step 3: she forgot to take the square root.[[/if]][[if test="is(er = 3)"]]Achieng's mistake is in step 4: she chose the wrong sign for the quadrant.[[/if]]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: find the mistake in a sine calculation. Entry: cos x, quadrant, error (1 subtracted cos x; 2 no square root; 3 wrong sign). Source: original. */
L: [[-0.28,2,1],[0.8,4,2],[-0.28,3,3],[0.96,4,1],[-0.8,2,2],[0.6,4,3],[-0.96,3,1],[0.6,4,2],[-0.6,3,3],[-0.8,3,2]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
g: L[ix][1]; qd: L[ix][2]; er: L[ix][3];
qword: if qd = 2 then "second" elseif qd = 3 then "third" else "fourth";
intv: if qd = 2 then "90^\\circ \\lt x \\lt 180^\\circ" elseif qd = 3 then "180^\\circ \\lt x \\lt 270^\\circ" else "270^\\circ \\lt x \\lt 360^\\circ";
ss: if qd = 2 then 1 else -1;
sword: if ss > 0 then "positive" else "negative";
v2: 1-g^2; sv: ss*sqrt(v2);
s2: if er = 1 then 1-g else v2;
s3: if er = 2 then v2 else sqrt(s2);
s4: if er = 3 then -ss*s3 else ss*s3;
opts: [["s1",false,"Step 1"],["s2",is(er=1),"Step 2"],["s3",is(er=2),"Step 3"],["s4",is(er=3),"Step 4"]];
ta1: first(mcq_correct(opts));
wstep: if er = 1 then "s3" else "s2";
wstep2: if er = 3 then "s3" else "s4";
d2: ss*v2; d3: float(ss*sqrt(1-g)); svoff: sv+0.1;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
